course: dictionary
lesson: 15136
title: Scanning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scanning means looking quickly over a page or a place to find one particular thing. You are not reading every word. Your eyes move fast, looking for a name, a number or a key word. «Scan the list for Sam's name» means look only for Sam.
explain: Your eyes skip past the words that do not matter until they find the one you need. Then stop scanning and read that part slowly. Scanning is different from skimming: skimming gives you the main idea of a text, while scanning hunts for one detail.
explain: Scanning can also mean using a machine. «The cashier scanned my apples and the price came up» means a machine read the barcode on the label. Scanning a page into a computer copies it, so the words can be stored there.
fact: Scanning means looking quickly over something to find one particular thing.
fact: «Scanning» can also mean using a machine to copy a picture or document into a computer.
fact: A barcode is scanned at the till so the shop knows the price of an item.
fact: In hospitals, a scan takes pictures of the inside of the body, such as an X-ray or an ultrasound.
fact: Be careful scanning a QR code you do not know, because it can send you to a website that is not safe.
exercise: «Scan the list for Sam's name.» What does scanning mean here? | Copying the whole list out by hand | Reading every word on the list slowly | *Looking quickly for one name | Drawing a picture of the list
exercise: «The cashier scanned my apples and the price came up.» What did the cashier do? | *Read the barcode with a machine | Cut the apples into pieces | Weighed the bag and wrote it down | Counted the apples by hand
exercise: What is the difference between scanning and reading a whole story? | Scanning is only for maps | *Scanning hunts for one detail, reading takes in the whole text | Scanning is slow and careful, reading is quick | They mean exactly the same thing
test: «The lifeguard scanned the sea for a swimmer in trouble.» What was the lifeguard looking for? | A shell on the sand | *A swimmer in trouble | A lost ball | A boat
test: To find the word «zebra» quickly in a dictionary, what should you do? | *Scan the page for the letter z | Read every page from the start | Ask a friend to read it aloud | Sing the alphabet slowly
exam: «The doctor sent Ravi for a scan of his knee.» In this sentence, scan means | *A machine picture of the inside of the body | A copy made on a printer | A sore place on the skin | A quick look for one word
